# Lavish plan gate (Phase ①)

Prakrit only. When the user is **Akhil**, skip this gate unless he asks.
See [`docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md) /
[`docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md).

Full standard: [`docs/agents/lavish-plan-standard.md`](docs/agents/lavish-plan-standard.md).

**Every prompt from the captain becomes a Lavish plan first.** A bug, an idea,
a screenshot, one line in chat — plan it, open it, iterate on it. **No product
code** until he says **`approved — build`**.

**Do not file a Linear ticket for it.** The plan is the artifact. File a ticket
only when he explicitly asks ("file a ticket", "log this in Linear").

## When the captain describes work

```bash
npm run workflow:plan -- --chat "<his exact message>"
```

That scaffolds `.lavish/plans/<ID>-<slug>/plan.html`, opens Lavish, and starts
the listener. Then **fill the scaffold** — it ships as a shell full of `slot`
placeholders and is not reviewable until you replace them.

Reply with: the plan path, one line on what it proposes, and **"waiting on your
edits / approved — build"**. Do not implement yet.

## The plan quality bar

| Tab | Must contain |
| --- | --- |
| Overview | today (verified in the running app) → after, in/out of scope |
| **UI** | the screen **mocked** in PropLane tokens — before/after, desktop/mobile, empty + loading + error |
| Build | file-by-file table, data/contract changes, order of work |
| Decide | open questions as pickable options, each with cost/benefit |
| Risks & tests | failure modes; real seeded data + edges, never `/demo` as proof |

The plan is the spec: **what it shows is exactly what gets built**. If build
forces a departure, update `plan.html`, re-open it, and say what moved.

It must stay **semi-interactive and editable** — tabs, before/after and
desktop/mobile toggles, `contenteditable` sections with *Queue my edits*, and
decision forms that submit once. All of it routes through
`window.lavish.queuePrompt`, which `npm run lavish:poll` drains.

## Lavish chat (mandatory — non-negotiable)

Captain feedback lives in **Lavish**, not chat alone. Open a plan without
polling and Lavish shows *"your agent is not listening"* — his annotations are lost.

**After opening a plan:**

1. Start the long poll — in Claude Code as a **tracked background** Bash task
   (`npm run lavish:poll -- --wait`); elsewhere `npm run lavish:listen`. One
   poller only; two race for the same delivery.
2. `npm run lavish:poll` before ending the turn — drains queued feedback.
3. Apply what came back, then `npm run lavish:poll -- --reply "…"` so he sees
   the answer where he wrote the note.

**Every later turn while `.lavish/active-session.json` exists:**

1. **First shell command:** `npm run lavish:poll`.
2. Apply his edits verbatim, re-open the same `plan.html` (never a second plan).
3. On **`approved — build`** → `npm run lavish:poll -- --clear`, then build.

| Command | When |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run lavish:listen` | right after opening a plan |
| `npm run lavish:poll` | first command of every turn |
| `npm run lavish:poll -- --reply "…"` | answer him inside the plan |
| `npm run lavish:poll -- --wait` | dedicated blocking wait |
| `npm run lavish:poll -- --clear` | after approval only |

**Never** tell the captain to annotate without having polled at least once.
**Never** end a plan-review turn without polling.

## Do not

- Write feature code before approval
- File a Linear ticket for the work (unless he asks)
- Ship a plan whose UI tab describes the screen instead of drawing it
- Leave `slot` placeholders in a plan you showed him
- Open Lavish and end the turn without polling
- Start a second plan for the same request

Skip the gate only on an explicit **`skip plan`** (hotfix).
